  "note": "Patcher matrix for B195, BUILT FROM main AT a955db4 (PR #370), seeded from the B194 matrix. ONE owner-reported bug fix over B194: invisible furniture stopped responding to a dropped villager when Transparent Graphics was enabled (Invisible Patio Table, Picnic Table, Spa Lounger, Yoga Equipment, Lounger, Ping-Pong Table), present on B192-B194 -- pre-existing, not a regression. Root cause: the patcher's drop dispatcher identifies the item through the stock PtOnFurniture hit-test, which samples sprite ALPHA (PixelIsVisible), so a fully transparent sprite resolves to nothing; native items (pools, couches) resolve by content-map geometry and never broke. Fix: when the stock resolver returns -1, VF2TransparentFurnitureItemAtPoint resolves the drop against the engine's OWN content block for that item -- LookupFurnitureInfo(item).contentBlocks[orientation], the block LoadFmap built for the orientation the placement record holds -- anchored exactly as CFurnitureManager::ApplyFmapContent anchors it (placement position minus the block origin, at the content map's 8 pixels per cell), with the hit being any cell the block occupies (ApplyContentBlock's own nonzero-cell rule) and the later slot winning on overlap. Nothing is baked at build time. Visible and native items are untouched; sprites stay fully transparent. Issue #369. See docs/B195-release-notes.md, which must not disagree with this field.",
